  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_pat",
  "prompt": "Which 2025 promotions failed to double unit sales? Take each promotion that started in 2025 (start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025) and compare the units sold on promotion with the baseline units. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0 units. Keep the promotions whose units on promotion are less than twice the baseline units. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, promo_units and baseline_units. Return one row for each promotion kept. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "promo_units",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "baseline_units",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
